    "result_text": "All 274 tests pass, including the new `Cp12Tests`. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-normalization rule in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (which handles `POST /api/owners`).\n\n**Changes to `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n\n1. In `addOwner`, added `owner.setCity(resolveCity(owner.getCity()))` right after mapping the incoming fields, so the normalized city flows into the stored owner, the customer code, and the response.\n\n2. Added two helpers:\n   - `resolveCity(String)` \u2014 scans existing owners for one whose city matches case-insensitively; if found, reuses that owner's exact spelling, otherwise title-cases the input. Null-safe.\n   - `titleCase(String)` \u2014 upper-cases the first letter of each whitespace-separated word and lower-cases the rest (e.g. `riverdale` \u2192 `Riverdale`, `san francisco` \u2192 `San Francisco`).\n\nThe rule satisfies the spec: `\"riverdale5\"` \u2192 `\"Riverdale5\"` on the first create, and a later create with `\"GREENVALE6\"` reuses the first owner's stored `\"Greenvale6\"` spelling. Existing tests using already-title-cased or seed cities (e.g. `Madison`, `Zedton`) are unaffected since normalizing them is a no-op.",
